        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nPerfect! Let me create a comprehensive summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the timestamp jump functionality for the osu! editor as described in the requirements. Here's what was added:\n\n### 1. **Enhanced Timestamp Parser** (`osu.Game/Rulesets/Edit/EditorTimestampParser.cs`)\n\n**New Features:**\n- **Multiple timestamp formats supported:**\n  - Full format: `mm:ss:mmm` or `mm:ss.mmm` (e.g., `\"01:23:456\"`)\n  - Abbreviated format: `mm:ss` (e.g., `\"10:44\"` meaning 10 minutes 44 seconds)\n  - Milliseconds only: numeric value (e.g., `\"12345\"` meaning 12.345 seconds)\n  - All formats support optional selection clauses in parentheses (e.g., `\"01:23:456 (1,2,3)\"`)\n\n- **Tolerant parsing:**\n  - Accepts incomplete timestamps (e.g., `\"1:2:3\"` is valid)\n  - Validates ranges: minutes < 600 (10 hours), seconds < 60, milliseconds < 1000\n  - Rejects clearly malformed inputs\n\n- **Public API exposed:**\n  - `TIME_REGEX` - Static regex for use by other modules (e.g., chat message formatter)\n  - `TryParse()` method with comprehensive XML documentation\n\n### 2. **Bottom Bar Timestamp Input** (`osu.Game/Screens/Edit/Components/TimeInfoContainer.cs`)\n\n**New UI Component:**\n- Added a `TimestampTextBox` input field below the track timer in the bottom bar\n- Users can type any valid timestamp format and press Enter to jump to that time\n- Clicking the input field selects all text for easy replacement\n- Placeholder text: \"Jump to time\"\n\n### 3. **Optional Error Notifications** (`osu.Game/Screens/Edit/Editor.cs` & `osu.Game/OsuGame.cs`)\n\n**Enhanced Error Handling:**\n- Added `showErrorNotification` parameter (defaults to `true`) to both `Editor.HandleTimestamp()` and `OsuGame.HandleTimestamp()`\n- When `false`, invalid timestamps fail silently without showing notifications\n- When `true` (default), displays user-visible error notification explaining the parsing failure\n- Maintains backward compatibility with existing code\n\n### 4. **Comprehensive Test Suite** (`osu.Game.Tests/Rulesets/Edit/EditorTimestampParserTest.cs`)\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n- Full format timestamps with various combinations\n- Abbreviated format timestamps\n- Milliseconds-only format timestamps\n- Timestamps with selection clauses\n- Invalid/malformed timestamps\n- Edge cases (boundary values)\n- Regex exposure verification\n\n### Key Design Decisions:\n\n1. **Backward Compatibility:** All existing functionality is preserved. The new parameter defaults to `true` for error notifications, maintaining current behavior.\n\n2. **Flexible Input:** The parser accepts timestamps in multiple common formats that users expect, making it more user-friendly.\n\n3. **Public API:** The `TIME_REGEX` is exposed for use by other modules like the chat message formatter, enabling clickable links that open the editor at specific times.\n\n4. **Selection Delegation:** When a selection clause is present, the editor delegates the exact selection logic to the active ruleset's `HitObjectComposer.SelectFromTimestamp()` method, allowing ruleset-specific behavior.\n\n5. **User Experience:** The bottom-bar input field provides immediate access to timestamp jumping without requiring external links or chat commands.\n\nThe implementation satisfies all requirements:\n- ✅ Accepts various timestamp formats (full, abbreviated, milliseconds-only)\n- ✅ Supports selection clauses in parentheses\n- ✅ Moves playback cursor to corresponding time\n- ✅ Highlights/references hit-objects when selection clause present\n- ✅ Optional error notification for invalid input\n- ✅ Tolerant parsing with validation\n- ✅ Exposed regex for chat message formatter\n- ✅ Accessible through public editor API\n- ✅ Observable UI behavior (instant playback position update)",
